.claude
.response
.plan

# Scratch measurement harnesses. Throwaway by design: each one answers a question
# once (a collision rate, a headroom limit, a window sweep) and the answer goes
# into ASSUMPTIONS.md as a numbered finding. The harness is the working, not the
# result -- keeping it would imply the numbers should be re-derived from it rather
# than re-measured, which is backwards.
.scratch/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Generator output. Byte-reproducible from a seed (tools/repro_check.py proves
# it), so versioning it would just add churn. Phase 13 can commit one frozen
# holdout run as a submission artifact if a judge should see the data without
# running anything.
data/
truth/

# Matcher and scorer output. Same reasoning: matches.json regenerates from the
# data plus a matcher, and tools/fixtures.py writes here by default.
out/

# Windows and OneDrive. Not hypothetical here: this working tree lives under
# OneDrive/Desktop, Explorer drops desktop.ini into any folder it has been asked
# to theme, and OneDrive writes sync-conflict copies next to the original rather
# than refusing the write.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Virtualenvs. The core pins nothing -- generator, matcher, scorer and queue are standard
# library only -- but pyproject.toml exists as of Phase 10 and pins one OPTIONAL extra
# (`pip install -e ".[llm]"`, for hisaab/explain alone), so a venv here is now a real
# possibility rather than a hypothetical. The manifest is committed; the environment is not.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor and IDE state. Personal to a machine, not to the project.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Caches belonging to tools this project does not currently use. Listed ahead of
# need: the phase that adds a linter or a test runner should not also have to
# notice its cache in the same diff.
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Log files, at any depth -- no log in this project is a source artifact. The
# measurement harnesses' own output is already covered by .scratch/ above.
*.log

# Secrets. Nothing in hisaab/ or tools/ reads a key -- Phase 9's smoke probe takes
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the environment and no file -- but Phase 9 is the phase
# that first made a key part of the workflow, so the ignore lands with it rather
# than in the phase that first writes one down. Listed before any .env exists, for
# the same reason as the caches above: the commit that adds a key path should not
# also be the commit that has to notice it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
